// wp_pool_depth — number of physical blocks in the hotframe pool.
//
// Fixed at 3 since AXVERITY_WRITE_PATH_SLICE_V1, chosen so that ejection is
// provably observable in one short run (THREE_BLOCKS_MEAN_EJECTION_IN_RUN):
// with three blocks a modest input forces a full rotation, so the free-pool
// backpressure path is exercised rather than merely present.
//
// AXVERITY_EXTENT_WRITE_PATH step 1 makes it a knob because it is a THROUGHPUT
// parameter that was chosen for TESTABILITY. The pool is what stands between
// the packer and a single flusher thread: the packer blocks in bchan_take on
// wp-free-pool until the flusher has reclaimed a block, so at depth 3 the
// writer can be at most 2 blocks ahead of the disk. At 16 KB blocks that is a
// 48 KB buffer; at a 4 MiB block it is 12 MB. Whether depth or capacity binds
// first is exactly what the step-6 sweep is for, and it cannot be swept while
// one of the two is structural.
//
// Minimum 3 is enforced at the mint site (src/mem_controller.m1), not here —
// a depth below 3 would stop exercising rotation, which is the property the
// original choice was protecting.
//
// Override: .axverity-store/config/pool_depth
fn wp_pool_depth(_u: Unit) -> Int {
  wp_cfg_get(Text("pool_depth"), Int(3))
}
